# System Admin (`@afenda/feature-system-admin`)

**ARCH-1006** (control plane) · **ARCH-1002** §7 (execution enforcement) · **ARCH-1003** (governed UI). Do not extend frozen kernel compat (**ARCH-1002** §7).

System Admin configures the law; Execution Kernel enforces it. Do not import `@afenda/feature-system-admin` from `@afenda/kernel`.

## Route shape (as-built)

| Layer | Location | Role |
| ----- | -------- | ---- |
| App Router | `(workspace)/[moduleId]/[...section]/page.tsx` | Thin entry when `moduleId === system-admin` |
| Section registry | `apps/erp/src/lib/system-admin-sections/registry.server.ts` | Slug → lazy `*.server.tsx` adapter |
| Manifest | `manifest.shared.ts` | Slug → `featureArea` under feature package |
| Feature | `packages/features/system-admin/src/<area>/` | Actions, data, policies, surfaces, components |

URL: `/system-admin/<section>` (route group omitted). Do not add `apps/erp/src/app/(workspace)/system-admin/` siblings — sections use the catch-all.

## Adapter pattern

Each `*.server.tsx` in `system-admin-sections/` is a thin adapter:

- Resolve org/session and execution context via `@afenda/kernel/server` or feature policies.
- Import UI copy + client islands from `@afenda/feature-system-admin/client`.
- Import loaders, actions, surface builders from `@afenda/feature-system-admin/server`.
- Compose `GovernedPatternCListSection` / Pattern A chrome from `@afenda/governed-surface/server`.

No business rules or Drizzle queries in adapters — keep them in the feature package.

## Feature package layout

Vertical buckets under `src/`: `users`, `memberships`, `roles`, `permissions`, `modules`, `capabilities`, `policies`, `approvals`, `audit-viewer`, `organization`, `security`, `integrations`, `diagnostics`, `lynx`, etc.

Each bucket: `actions/`, `data/`, `policies/`, `schemas/`, `contracts/`, `components/`, `surface/` as needed. Package-level `components/`, `overview/` for shared control-list helpers.

Export doors only: `.`, `./client`, `./server`, `./metadata` — never deep imports from app or other packages.

## Permissions & audit

- Guard reads and mutations with `requireExecutionPermission` (or feature policy wrappers).
- Capability keys: `system-admin.<domain>.read|manage|…` — keep keys when folding routes (`/raf`); do not delete capability fallbacks without user direction.
- Every mutation writes structured audit via execution audit helpers; use domain-specific audit actions from contracts.

## Governed surfaces

- Pattern C lists: server window + `build*ListSurface` → `GovernedPatternCListSection`.
- Trailing actions: serializable `Cell` from client registry — never `trailingColumn.render`.
- Batch independent page loads with `Promise.all`.

